{
  "quest.416DF22D3068D0F2.quest_desc": [
    "Magic Mirrors are portals to transfer Items! \\n\\nSimply place one down, then Shift Right Click on that Mirror with another Mirror to Link them. \\n\\nOnce Linked, place down the 2nd Mirror and you can now toss Items into one Mirror and out the other. \\n\\nOnly Items, not Mobs or anything else. Just Items. \\n\\nThere's also a Hand-held version that you can Link to a Mirror and use to toss Items from your Inventory to the Mirror.",
  ],
  "quest.1AFD7D4D8A73BD9F.quest_subtitle": "Earth",
  "quest.29CC17333C92174E.title": "&8Primal Crusher",
  "quest.072217F29C63E436.title": "&bPraemunio",
  "quest.579ACBFD4C70BBD2.title": "&4Crimson Rites",
  "quest.04DD92D1F0039BA4.quest_subtitle": "Aura",
  "quest.27729CC2CC9E720B.quest_desc": [
    "&dCausality Collapsers&r are quite dangerous... so let's throw one into the even more dangerous thing! \\n\\nRight Clicking with a &dCausality Collapser&r will shoot it like a Fireball. If it hits anything it will cause an Explosion. \\n\\nIf it hits a &5&lFlux Rift&r it will Collapse the &5&lRift&r. This will cause a number of Explosions and will Drop Items once it is gone. \\n\\nThe amount of Explosions and Items depends on how big the &5&lRift&r was. Bigger the &5&lRift&r, bigger the booms, and better the Items. \\n\\nEverytime you'll get &8Void Seeds&r but if the &5&lRift&r is big enough and you're lucky enough you might get &zPrimordial Motes&r.",
  ],
  "quest.5EE4441CED3C2D1D.quest_desc": [
    "&dAura Nodes&r spawn randomly throughout the &2&lWorld&r... you'll just need &6Goggles of Revealing&r to actually see them. \\n\\nThese will always spawn with &eAspects&r, which we can use on &3Wand&r on them to take out the &eAspects&r. This will drain the &dNode&r though unless you have certain Upgrades or Machines. \\n\\n&dNodes&r will eventually gain more of the &eAspects&r they spawned with (unless you took every single bit of &eAspect&r from them). \\n\\nYou can learn the Node Preserver so when you use &3Wands&r (that aren't made of Iron Caps or Wood Rods) will always leave 1 &eAspect&r in the &dNode&r so you don't Drain them. \\n\\nThere's different levels to them, their levels affect their behavior with &eAspects&r and other &dNodes&r. You can use a &6Thaumometer&r on them to learn what Level they are.",
  ],
  "quest.3B7679135A74BBBA.title": "&2Zombies&r but madder than usual",
  "quest.46EAA6889A904314.title": "&7Metallum",
  "quest.08DCE3A8415F2019.quest_desc": [
    "Mixing some &8Void Seeds&r in a &7&lCrucible&r with &7Metallum&r and &5Vitium&r will make &8Void Metal&r. \\n\\n&8Void Metal&r can make Tools, Armor, and even Machines!",
  ],
  "quest.476556F0B06ADCA9.title": "&7Volatus",
  "quest.5DD51B2E0D59AE90.title": "&8Deconstruction Table",
  "quest.6958759ABD603C22.quest_subtitle": "Change",
  "quest.225993D2A2868AF4.title": "&3Wands",
  "quest.5998B1AFFDA09725.quest_desc": [
    "&5Venting Ports&r take out a fraction of &5Flux&r generated from Smelters. \\n\\n&cSlurry Pumps&r will increase how fast the &cSmelter&r works. \\n\\nYou can add a combination of 3 of them because they need to be added to the sides of the &cSmelter&r.",
  ],
  "quest.29367282B57653A1.quest_desc": [
    "Gaining a &dNode Stabilizer&r teaches us more about the &dNodes&r. \\n\\n&dNodes&r have 4 levels: Bright, Fading, Pale, and None. They also have multiple different types: Normal, Hungry, Unstable, Tainted, Dark, and Pure. \\n\\nMost will just be Normal with None. But some might be a little more dangerous. \\n\\n&dNode Stabilizers&r can be placed under a &dNode&r to keep it safe and alone. It won't give &eVis&r to other &dNodes&r or take &eVis&r from other &dNodes&r. \\n\\nIf it is used on an &dUnstable Node&r it will prevent the &dNode&r from randomly losing &eVis&r and might even make them stable! \\n\\nThere is the downside of it halving the &eVis&r recharge rate...",
  ],
  "task.5325DC34EFAEB150.title": "AllRightsReserved",
  "quest.4F6D870249CE2F17.quest_desc": [
    "Sorry guys we got to follow the lore, we can't just skip past and tell you how to do everything right away. \\n\\nTake a nap after taking some &eCrystals&r home and you'll learn from a Dream of what &dSalis Mundus&r is. \\n\\nOr atleast how we make it!",
  ],
  "quest.08F7DB9115F6525E.quest_desc": [
    "Instability is a problem with the &5&lArcane Infuser&r. Apparently it's more topsy-turner than a top! \\n\\nInstability is affected by 1. Recipes 2. Symmetry 3. Items and Blocks near. \\n\\nSome Recipes are much more Unstable than others, it'll tell you it in JEI. When a Recipe is Unstable, the &5&lInfuser&r will start blasting off Items and will ruin the Recipe. \\n\\nSymmetry is important for keeping everything balanced. &7Pedestals&r should be on the same spot of both sides of the &5&lInfuser&r and if there is 2 Items in a Recipe they should be on parallel sides. If there's just one Item of a certain type then your best bet is placing it in the middle column. \\n\\nSome Items can be placed around the &5&lInfuser&r (also with Symmetry) to keep things Balanced. Some stuff like Candles to the best ones which are &cStabilizers&r. &cStabilizers&r will take out the Instability and turn it into &5Flux&r. In order to work though, you'll need to connect &cRedstone Inlays&r between the &cStabilizers&r and &7Arcane Pedestals&r.",
  ],
  "quest.7CF40FC87BE0BF3F.quest_subtitle": "Order",
  "quest.62C846C67983F020.title": "&bGelum",
  "quest.3135F77E4AB99790.title": "&dCausality Collapser",
  "quest.29AA2F2E28439514.quest_desc": [
    "Normal &dNodes&r not working for you? Why not Energize them! \\n\\nFirst, Stabilize the &dNode&r. Then, place a &dNode Transducer&r above the &dNode&r and power it with &cRedstone&r. \\n\\nThis will deplete the &dNode&r and after awhile it will bring it back Energized. &dEnergized Nodes&r will take &eVis&r from the &dAura&r and give it out to &dVis Relays&r nearby. \\n\\nThis can be connected to Machines like &eVis Rechargers&r or &5Flux Scrubbers&r to power them!",
  ],
  "quest.68AD04436F09B39A.title": "&bEthereal Bloom",
  "quest.0F311C523A9ADC5F.title": "&eLux",
  "quest.2CDB0970A097C0AC.quest_subtitle": "Animal",
  "quest.75EFD75C1C7644B2.quest_desc": [
    "&bShimmerleafs&r are rare Flowers found in &bMagical Forests&r. \\n\\nThey're used in a few Recipes, mainly: Quicksilver and &bEthereal Blooms&r.",
  ],
  "quest.547259A485A7BDCA.title": "&5Vitium",
  "quest.7CA7F4F31BC570D3.title": "Moving &eEssentia",
  "quest.401787DC43ECEFCD.quest_subtitle": "Ability",
  "quest.32FA68F06F6C4EA0.quest_desc": [
    "In order to start milking Items for &eEssentia&r we'll need 2 Machines (for now), the &cEssentia Smelter&r and the &eArcane Alembic&r. \\n\\nPlace the &eAlembic&r above the &cSmelter&r to set it up. Toss Furnace Fuel in the &cSmelter&r and any Item that has &eEssentia&r you want to break down, into the &cSmelter&r. \\n\\nAfter some time it will collect the &eEssentia&r into the &eAlembic&r which will turn it into the raw &eEssentia&r we can finally move around with &bJars&f, &bPhials&f, and &eTubes&r. \\n\\nShift Right Clicking the &eAlembic&r will void all &eEssentia&r in it.",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/thaumaturge/thaum_smelter.png width:125 height:100 align:center click_action:none:}",
  ],
  "quest.1B67B647F51178A4.title": "&dNode in a Jar",
  "quest.075312A557578AE0.quest_subtitle": "Glass",
  "quest.3E311C85E71F6E5E.title": "&2Greatwood",
  "quest.10CB678409E37068.quest_subtitle": "Alchemy",
  "quest.04DD92D1F0039BA4.title": "&dAurum",
  "quest.76586B14AA42057C.quest_desc": [
    "&5Flux&r is dangerous for our Worlds but we just can't stop doing Magic! \\n\\nWe need to get rid of it... a &5Flux Condenser&r will help! \\n\\nThe &5Condenser&r will take &eEssentia&r Piped in from the sides, doesn't matter what type. Then, it will transform &5Flux&r into &5Vitium&r and Pipe that below it. \\n\\nIn order to work it will need a &5Flux Condenser Lattice&r on top of it. Or 8. The more you have the quicker it will work, but it might also clog more. \\n\\nWhen they're Clogged they need to be either replaced or you can use an Essentia Filter on them to clear them out.",
  ],
  "quest.56CA8FE4F47FD30E.title": "Growing &eCrystals&r?",
  "quest.08BD38B3ED25D0F7.quest_desc": [
    "Upgrading our &8Void Metal Armor&r will give us &8Void Thaumaturge Armor&r. \\n\\nThese give &4Warp&r and will regenerate Durability over time. \\n\\nThe Armor gives a &eVis&r Discount and the &8Hood&r comes with &6Goggles of Revealing&r.",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/thaumaturge/thaum_voidrobes.png width:100 height:150 align:center click_action:none:}",
  ],
  "quest.7CF40FC87BE0BF3F.title": "Ordo",
  "quest.667DE2DC3C19B6DF.title": "&5Flux",
  "quest.1B67B647F51178A4.quest_desc": [
    "Surrounding a &dNode&r with a cube of Glass, Topping it with Wood Slabs, then pressing your &3Wand&r to the Structure will turn the &dNode&r into a &dNode in a Jar&r! \\n\\nThis &dNode&r will go down a Level but it can now be moved around. You can break and move the Jar with no issues. \\nYou can Shift Right Click the Jar to reload your &3Wand&r with the &eVis&r, just don't forget to Shift. \\n\\nJust Right Clicking the &dJar&r with your &3Wand&r will break the &dJar &rand release the &dNode&r.",
  ],
  "quest.6BEA915DB03C70E0.title": "&bWarded Jar",
  "quest.1D892E8692E13871.quest_subtitle": "Death",
  "quest.23CAD6414B20408A.quest_subtitle": "Machine",
  "quest.5170CC16613804DC.quest_desc": [
    "&2&lArcane Workbenches&r are magical Crafting Tables. \\n\\nThey'll Craft Items using a Cost of &dAura&r and &eVis&r. &eVis&r from &eCrystals&r or a Wand placed in it. \\n\\nIt only needs the Primal Aspects, whether that's a good thing or a bad thing is up to you. \\n\\nThis will be needed to Craft most Items from &5&lThaumaturge&r.",
  ],
  "quest.771F42A1E9E9A7BB.title": "&4Warp",
  "quest.39C080EE72182A8B.quest_desc": [
    "Wireless or I guess Pipeless &eEssentia&r transfer. \\n\\nThe &eFilling Essentia Transfuser&r will take &eEssentia&r from &ePipes&r and give it out to &bJars&r up to 16 Blocks from where it is aimed. \\n\\nThe &eEmptying Transfuser&r will pull &eEssentia&r from &bJars&r and bring it into the &ePipes&r or Machine it is connected to.",
  ],
  "quest.09FD966539DA9960.quest_desc": [
    "&eEssentia Mirrors&r work similar to Magic Mirrors just moving &eEssentia&r instead of Items. \\n\\nPlace one down, then Shift Right Click with another &eMirror&r to Link them, and place that &eMirror&r down as well. \\n\\nExcept these don't work with &eEssentia Tubes&r they need their &eEssentia&r more free-flowing... like what you'd see with the &5&lArcane Infuser&r!",
  ],
  "quest.7688896C886CBFF3.title": "&2Zombie Brain",
  "quest.521EE1FA4C016AAA.quest_desc": [
    "Changing out the Arms is the biggest change to a &cGolems&r job ability. \\n\\nThe Fine Manipulators makes it so the &cGolems&r Arms are more precise but also delicate. The &cGolem&r will be weaker but more accurate. \\n\\nClaw Arms do the opposite of Fine Manipulators, it gives up accuracy for raw power! The &cGolem&r will now be Clumsy but can Fight and will put up a good Fight. \\n\\nBreaker Arms are like handing a &cGolem&r some Pickaxes. They're made for Mining and can Break most Blocks now. They can also do a lot of Damage but aren't inherently Fighters. \\n\\nDart Launchers will let our &cGolem&r attack at range, with no worry of Ammo. It comes will come with the ability to Fight but also losses some of its Strength.",
  ],
  "quest.667DE2DC3C19B6DF.quest_desc": [
    "Screwing with Magic produces &5Flux&r. Sometimes it is unavoidable... \\n\\n&5Flux&r affects a certain part of the &dAura&r, you can see the damage when wearing &6Goggles of Revealing&r. The more &5Flux&r in an area, the worse the effects. \\nIt starts off with &5Goo &fand &5Plume&r. &5Plume&r just flies into the atmosphere, just normal pollution. The &5Goo&r though will spread and stick to everything. You'll also gain &5Vis Exhaust&r while touching it. \\n\\nThe more &5Flux&r, the more dangerous and corrupted your area will get. It will start corrupting Grass and Trees to Mobs to even the Nodes will become corrupted. \\n\\nMobs that are covered in &5Taint&r or that come from &5Taint&r will be Hostile and will give you &5Flux Taint&r Effect which acts like Poison.",
  ],
  "quest.04D1E90DA88C4870.quest_desc": [
    "I don't think I'll ever be able to remember this ones name... \\n\\nBut if you attach these to the &eThaumatorium&r it will add 2 more Recipes it can make at a time. Usually it will only do 1 at a time, but with up to 5 of these things attached we can do 15! \\n\\nWell, you can't add any Tubes if you use all 5... so I guess we're limited to 13.",
  ],
  "quest.1D42E0BA24801446.title": "&2Boots of the Traveller",
  "quest.3F452025833A266C.title": "&8Exanimis",
  "quest.7BC7861D2AFF266C.title": "&6Ignis",
  "quest.401787DC43ECEFCD.title": "&bPotentia",
  "quest.5643D8B1506FF9B8.title": "Making &3Spells",
  "quest.6F4E1656EE7D9B1F.title": "&8Vacuos",
  "quest.206A1DC13EF3DE0D.title": "&8Tenebrae",
  "quest.26F5B01872848BCF.quest_subtitle": "Water",
  "quest.58C818AC4DCC359F.title": "Making Machines",
  "quest.0B90BDB60F42E8F9.quest_desc": [
    "Tossing some &dDust&r on a Bookshelf will turn all 6 Books and even the Wood Frame into a singular Guide Book, the &6&lThaumonomicon&r. \\n\\nYou'll need it to learn what to Craft and Research. \\n\\nI guess you can just follow the Book and ignore these Quests entirely... but then you'll miss out on Rewards and my charm!",
  ],
  "quest.4F7A87C87431E691.title": "&3Focus Pouch",
  "task.58D5B4F7EFA569CB.title": "Void Gears",
  "quest.18250BCA57DE2BBE.quest_desc": [
    "Research is a huge part of &5&lThaumaturge&r, specifically the progressing further part. \\n\\nFirst, Craft some &0Scribing Tools&r and gather Paper. We'll need both. \\n\\nPlace down 2 &6Wood Tables&r next to each other than use a &0Scribing Tool&r on them to create a &e&lResearch Table&r. Before we start using it, let's do some Research! \\n\\nIf you have Paper and &0Scribing Tools&r in your Inventory, then you can Open your &6Thaumomonicon&r and Click on the Research prompts when they are available. This will use up the Paper and some of your &0Scribing Tool&r. \\n\\nNow we can go back to the &e&lResearch Table&r. Here we will see all &eAspects&r we've learned from using the &6Thaumometer&r on Blocks/Items/Mobs. \\n\\nYou can Click them into the bottom part to combine them into new &eAspects&r. These Recipes can be confusing to follow, you can look at the &eAspects&r in the &6Thaumomonicon&r or even use the Quests at the top of the Quest Page to see the Recipes! \\n\\nThese are also important when using Research Notes. In the &e&lResearch Table&r, place down the Research Note next to the Button with the &6Thaumomonicon&r on it. This will open up the board on the right that we'll need to complete to finish Researching! \\n\\nIf the &eAspects&r show a \"?\" then you haven't Researched it yet. If you can see all of them, you'll need to place &eAspects&r that you've learned into the Hexagons to connect them. \\n\\nUse all the space you need until their connected. Once done, just Right Click with the completed Discovery.",
  ],
  "quest.367945E9E945170F.quest_desc": [
    "The &eCentrifuge&r will take &eEssentia&r and break it into half of a different &eEssentia&r it is made of. \\n\\nObviously only &eCompound Essentia&r can be processed through, not &ePrimal&r. \\n\\nIt will randomly pick 1 of the &eEssentia&r it is made of to be left over and be Piped out of the top of the &eCentrifuge&r. \\n\\nThe other will be lost to space and time!",
  ],
  "quest.00AA47CC2B4DF9E6.quest_subtitle": "Desire",
  "quest.1D42E0BA24801446.quest_desc": [
    "The &2Boots of the Traveller&r need &eVis&r added to them to work. Either from a &bJar&r or &eVis Recharger&r. \\n\\nOnce they have &eVis&r in them you can wear and use them. When wearing them you'll Run faster, Jump higher, and Swim better. ",
  ],
  "quest.42A6111B27289BCF.title": "&7Motus",
  "quest.5D2113E957C8485C.quest_desc": [
    "dUnderground (in new Chunks) you might come across some &eCrystals&r. \\n\\n&eAir&f, &6Fire&f, &bWater&f, &aEarth&f, &8Entropy&r, and Order Crystals spawning on the walls and floors of Caves. \\n\\nYou can pick these up with your Hands. They're the start to &5&lThaumaturge&r! ",
  ],
  "quest.15FF21AF6F1C8896.title": "&6Sanity Checker",
  "quest.56A0F8E3AE0C8ACF.quest_desc": [
    "&dSanity Soap&r is applied by Holding Right Click. \\n\\nIt will first remove &4Temporary Warp&r, then it has a chance to remove normal &4Warp&r. \\n\\nSome &4Warp&r even the &dSanity Soap&r can't remove... ",
  ],
  "quest.5C571F69FF4677D6.title": "&6Lamps",
  "quest.367945E9E945170F.title": "&eEssentia Centrifuge",
  "quest.206A1DC13EF3DE0D.quest_subtitle": "Darkness",
  "quest.49399AC18569034E.title": "&8Void Gear",
  "quest.08DCE3A8415F2019.title": "&8Void Metal",
  "quest.6D4501C08A83DA60.title": "&5&lFlux Rifts",
  "quest.00AA47CC2B4DF9E6.title": "&eDesiderium",
  "quest.190752598FDCE408.title": "&cGolem&r Body",
  "quest.08DD0CF854889F50.title": "&eThaumatorium",
  "quest.7BED978C9F18F48A.title": "&aSensus",
  "quest.68AD04436F09B39A.quest_desc": [
    "&bEthereal Blooms&r are Magical upgrades of &bShimmerleaf&r. \\n\\nWhen placed down, they'll clean up any &5Taint Blocks&r near them. \\n\\nTheir range is about 8 Blocks so if your magical mess is bigger than that, then you might need more than one. \\n\\nThey won't take &5Flux&r out of the &dAura&r, only &5Taint&r.",
  ],
  "quest.662F077AD22AEA1B.quest_desc": [
    "Upgrades are optional bonuses to our &cGolems&r. \\n\\nArmor Plating will make our &cGolems&r Armored and they will Repair themselves twice as fast, but they will go up a Weight level. \\n\\nThe Aggression Module allows the &cGolem&r to fight Mobs, no longer being Passive. \\n\\nThe Carry Frame will double the amount of Items the &cGolem&r can hold.",
  ],
  "quest.32FA68F06F6C4EA0.title": "&eEssentia Smelting",
  "quest.615179FA7C209DE0.quest_desc": [
    "Legs are needed to move around, the type will depend how and where. \\n\\nA Uni-wheel gives it a single Wheel instead of Legs. This will let your &cGolem&r move very quickly, just not well up things. \\n\\nClimbing Legs will let &cGolems&r climb up Walls we normally can't. There doesn't seem to be any downside to these except for the cost. \\n\\nThe Levitation Module will forget about Gravity entirely, instead choosing to Fly! At the cost of Speed and &cGolem&r Durability.",
  ],
  "quest.7ABF6AC8890537EB.title": "&dCognitio",
  "quest.7B659C1D725BDEB2.quest_desc": [
    "&6Goggles of Revealing&r are pretty much required. \\n\\nWhen worn you can see the number stats of multiple sources from &5&lThaumaturge&r. Like &eVis&r and &5Flux&r in &dAura&r. \\n\\nYou'll also see more information when viewing Machines and Nodes. Speaking of Nodes, you can only see them when using the &6Goggles&r. To make it easier to find them, they will also show through Blocks.",
  ],
  "quest.74F8FF27C911E33F.quest_desc": [
    "&bSilverwood&r is a very rare Tree. I have only found them in &bMagical Forests&r from &5&lThaumaturge&r. \\n\\nThe Trees spawn from a normal Sapling and wild ones will have a Pure Node within them. \\n\\nThey're very magical, even the Wood helps with Enchanting!",
  ],
  "quest.611EE34F11D4B615.quest_desc": [
    "&5Thaumium Fortress Armor&r is an upgraded version of &5Thaumium Helmets&f, &5Chestplates&f, and &5Leggings&r. No Boots, you'll have to fill in with some other Boots. \\n\\nAll 3 Pieces have 16 Armor Points and 9 Armor Toughness. They each give Protections against Magic Damage, Fire Damage, and others. They do even more Protection when Equipped with each other. \\n\\n&5Infusing&r the &5Helmet&r will give it extra effects. Using it with the &6Goggles of Revealing&r give the effect of both the &5Helmet&r and &6Goggles&r. The rest are Faceplates. \\n\\nGrinning Devil will decrease the effects of &4Warp&r. Angry Ghost might give the &0Wither&r Effect to things that Hit you. And Sipping Fiend gives you Lifesteal!",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/thaumaturge/thaum_fortress.png width:100 height:150 align:center click_action:none:}",
  ],
  "quest.79762364D0FCC878.quest_desc": [
    "Think of a normal &eEssentia Smelter&r... but faster!",
  ],
  "quest.7CFEC5BFC58E382C.quest_desc": [
    "&5Taint Seeds&r can Spawn from Events with the &5&lFlux Rift&r. \\n\\nThey have 75 &4Hearts&r and only enjoy one thing in life, that being to spread &4Taint&r. \\n\\n&5Taint Seeds&r will constantly spread &5Taint&r around them as long as they are alive. \\n\\nGetting near them will provoke them, they'll start spitting &5Taint&r at you. Killing them doesn't Drop anything either, it just gives a sense of feeling that you're protecting your World from the spread of &5Taint&r. \\n\\nWe think that's rewarding enough!",
  ],
  "quest.7424F6181F12F72E.title": "&3Focal Manipulator",
  "quest.330B0DD53138E3D5.quest_desc": [
    "&5&lThaumaturge&r uses a bunch of different Items and &aAspects&r but 2 reaccuring Ingots are &6Brass&r and &5Thaumium&r. \\n\\nThankfully they use Tags for Recipes so we can make &6Brass&r any way you want to. \\n\\n&5Thaumium&r has one specific Recipe which involves the &7&lCrucible&r. \\n\\nYou might want to make some, you'll need it for a few Recipes.",
  ],
  "quest.19932A116C8EE714.title": "&5Taintacles",
  "task.50079EA5547841C5.title": "Golem Upgrades",
  "quest.04D1E90DA88C4870.title": "Mne... thing that allows us to use more Recipes",
  "quest.5D2113E957C8485C.title": "&5&lThaumaturge",
  "quest.1EE97E362E14A14D.title": "&eRecharge Pedestal",
  "quest.29367282B57653A1.title": "Types of &dNodes&r and Farming them",
  "quest.5644DF859A83B0CB.title": "&bGlass Phials",
  "quest.03ED04CD00BB0EF9.quest_desc": [
    "The &bWorkbench Charger&r can be placed on &2&lArcane Workbenches&r and &bFocal Manipulators&r to increase the area where they will get &dAura&r from. \\n\\nFrom 1 Chunk, to 9!",
  ],
  "quest.1D892E8692E13871.title": "&4Mortuus",
  "quest.4F7A87C87431E691.quest_desc": [
    "Holding a whole bunch of different &3Foci&r for all your different needs, quickly becomes troublesome. \\n\\nEach &3Focus&r takes up a whole Inventory Slot! \\n\\nWith the &3Focus Pouch &rthat'll change it to 18 &3Foci&r per Slot! \\n\\nJust toss them in the &3Pouch&r and you can use them with your &3Wands&r just like normal!",
  ],
  "quest.32791F4495701E7A.quest_subtitle": "Entrapment",
  "task.5D2625AE94E3131C.title": "Vis Crystals",
  "quest.6D4501C08A83DA60.quest_desc": [
    "I didn't know a better way to make the Quest to observe &5&lFlux Rifts&r, the fact they're barely Blocks or Entities makes it difficult. I figured collecting &5Vitium Crystals&r is fair since you'll need a ton of &5Flux&r to have one appear. \\n\\n&5&lFlux Rifts&r will spawn when the &5Flux&r has exceeded 75% of the &eVis Capacity&r. Aka a ton of &5Flux&r. You'll know when spawns when the screen tells you in &5Purple Text&r \"You feel a sudden release of magical tension nearby\". \\n\\n&5&lFlux Rifts&r look like cracks in reality itself. A black Void similar to &d&lThe Ends&r sky, surrounded by a white fog in a twisting line. \\n\\nIf you are wearing &6Goggles of Revealing&r you'll be able to see them through Blocks. They also can't spawn next to other &5&lFlux Rifts&r, which trust me is a good thing. \\n\\n&5&lFlux Rifts&r will Break any Blocks they touch and Void any Items in them. Any Mobs or Players will be Damaged by them when they touch them regardless of Protection. \\n\\n&5&lFlux Rifts&r will grow and spread when there is enough &5Flux&r. They will take in some of the &5Flux&r from around to grow. But the bigger they get the more unstable they can get. \\n\\nIf the &5&lFlux Rift&r seems to be wiggling that means it is getting unstable and it will cause an Event. \\n\\nThese Events (and &5&lRifts&r themselves) aren't good... so let's try to either get rid of them or atleast Stabilize them!",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/thaumaturge/thaum_rift.png width:100 height:100 align:center click_action:none:}",
  ],
  "quest.611EE34F11D4B615.title": "&5Thaumium Fortress Armor",
  "quest.3F452025833A266C.quest_subtitle": "Undead",
  "quest.56CA8FE4F47FD30E.quest_desc": [
    "Now with &5Arcane Infusion&r we can Farm &eCrystals&r! \\n\\nNow we can Craft the &eCrystal&r bunches ourselves, place them down and watch them Grow. \\n\\nWe can only make the 6 Primal Aspects and &5Vitium&r.",
  ],
  "quest.690BC109F680186E.title": "&9Instrumentum",
  "task.38F5F9C87769E82C.title": "Void Robes",
  "quest.5B82CF209A6EF130.quest_desc": [
    "&7&lCrucibles&r are made when you use &dSalis Mundus&r on a Cauldron. \\n\\nTo use it, you'll need a &6Heat Source&r beneath it and &bWater&r within it. &6Heat Sources&r like &6Fire&r, Campfires, or even Nitor. \\n\\nOnce the &bWater&r is Boiling you can toss in Items to add different &eAspects&r needed to use it. (You'll need to be wearing &6Goggles of Revealing&r to see the exact amounts). \\n\\nThen, toss in Items to finish certain Recipes. ",
  ],
  "quest.58C818AC4DCC359F.quest_desc": [
    "&5&lThaumaturge&r has Machines, ones more complicated than a fancy Crafting Table or fancy Cauldron. \\n\\nFor these we'll need &8Alchemical Constructions&r! \\n\\nThere are also Multiblocks, all of them have specific building instructions and will need you to use &dSalis Mundus&r on it to finish the Build.",
  ],
  "quest.5C571F69FF4677D6.quest_desc": [
    "The &2Lamp of Growth&r will take in &2Herba&r in order to give off Light and a Speed growth to nearby &2Plants&r. \\n\\nWhile the &4Lamp of Fertility&r will use &eDesiderium&r to woo Mobs without needing Items. If there's 8 of that Mob near the &4Lamp&r though it won't Breed them.",
  ],
  "quest.330B0DD53138E3D5.title": "&5&lThaumaturge&r Metals",
  "quest.771F42A1E9E9A7BB.quest_desc": [
    "&4Warp&r is what happens to you when you mess around with stuff you shouldn't. \\n\\nI say shouldn't as in the magic gods or whatever don't want you to mess with but in order to progress you'll need to. \\n\\nSome Recipes and Researches will give you &4Warp&r. \\n\\n&4Warp&r can be temporary, this will only give a little bit of it which will disappear over time. The other types of &4Warp&r will need you to use &dSanity Soap&r or &6Purifying Fluid&r to get rid. And some can't be removed at all! \\n\\nThe more &4Warp&r you get the less Sanity you have. This will come with horrible effects. \\n\\n&dBath Salts&r can help to protect you from gaining &4Warp&r, toss it in &bWater&r and it will (slowly) form &6Purifying Fluid&r. Hop in and you'll get the Warp Ward Effect.",
  ],
  "quest.690BC109F680186E.quest_subtitle": "Tool",
  "quest.0B90BDB60F42E8F9.title": "&6&lThaumonomicon",
  "quest.62C846C67983F020.quest_subtitle": "Cold",
  "quest.2BECD3C37FDD675F.title": "&5Taint Crawlers",
  "quest.7EFC0C6396E0C483.quest_desc": [
    "The &2Sword of the Zephyr&r does slightly more Damage and it will gain a Wind ability when you Hold Right Click. This will Block Damage, move Mobs away from you, and raise you into the air. You can turn this off by Shift Right Clicking with it. \\n\\nThe &cPickaxe of the Core&r works like a &bDiamond Pickaxe&r with 2 Special Abilities. 1. It might randomly Drop Native Ores instead of Raw Ores. 2. Holding Right Click will make it point out Ores through Blocks nearby. \\n\\nThe &bAxe of the Stream&r won't Cut the Log you're aiming at, instead it'll start from the Logs highest from the one you're Cutting. You can Hold Right Click for it to vacuum Items toward it. \\n\\nThe &5Shovel of the Earthmover&r will Dig in a 3x3 Area. It can also place some Blocks in a 3x3 area of the same Block you use it on. \\n\\nThe &5Hoe of Growth&r (I guess some can change) will till in a 3x3 area. It can also Right Click a Plant to give it Bonemeal at the cost of Durability. \\n\\nThe &2Spear of the Firmament&r is a lot like a normal Spear, just more fun! When Mobs are Killed by it they'll Drop some &eAspects&r. When Jousting with the &2Spear&r it will toss whatever it Hits into the Air. Faster you they're Hit, the higher they go!",
  ],
  "quest.5B698B4F90F859F5.quest_desc": [
    "Like any Pipes (or atleast most) there are other versions that do more than just what the normal ones do. \\n\\n&eValves&r can be Right Clicked to close off the movement of &eEssentia&r through the &ePipes&r. \\n\\n&eRestricted&r ones act like normal, just with half the Suction power. \\n\\n&eFilters&r can be handed a &eVis Crystal&r or &bPhial&f full of &eEssentia&r to only allow that certain &eAspect&r through the &ePipes&r. \\n\\n&eOne ways&r will just take Suction from the direction the Blue side is on. ",
  ],
  "quest.08F0B67D02683C3A.quest_desc": [
    "&cControl Seals&r are how we order our &cGolems&r to do... well pretty much everything! \\n\\nThey are placed down on Blocks and you can only see them when you're Holding a &cGolem&r, &cControl Seal&r, or the &7Golemancer's Bell&r. \\n\\n&cControl Seals&r have functions and settings, we're going to talk about the settings in the next Quest here is mostly for the actual functions. \\n\\nWhen &cGolems&r are placed down they make that spot their Home. If their Home is in range of a &cControl Seal&r they will follow the &cSeals&r Order, if possible. \\n\\nWe say if possible because some &cControl Seals&r require specific &cGolem&r types, like ones that aren't Clumsy. \\n\\nWhen the &cGolem&r is in range of any &cControl Seals&r it will preform the task the &cSeal&r asks them to do. If there is mulitiple &cSeals&r in range it will do all of them in an order based on Priorities set in the &cSeal&r. \\n\\n&cGolems&r can also be Dyed Colors to coordinate them to specific &cSeals&r. \\n\\nTo pick up &cSeals&r simply Shift Right Click them with the &7Golemancer's Bell&r or Break the Block they're connected to.",
  ],
  "quest.7424F6181F12F72E.quest_desc": [
    "The &3Focal Manipulator&r is where the fun really begins for making &3Focus Spells&r. \\n\\nHere we can see our Inventory and the workshop. Just toss your &3Focus&r in and start tinkering. \\n\\nAt the top you can see the current &3Focus&r, change its name, and set it all in stone. \\n\\nOn the left we have the parts of each &3Focus&r. Delivery, Effect, Modifier, and Flow. Delivery is who or where, Effect is what it does, Modifier is how or how much, and Flow is when. \\n\\nThe middle is the actual chain of the &3Focus&r. It is where you connect the parts you selected and order them. \\n\\nOn the right is the cost and availability of each part selected. This also includes the Power of each part. \\n\\nIf it all works out perfectly you can pay your &aExperience&r and click the Checkmark to finish your &3Focus&r!",
  ],
  "quest.1EE97E362E14A14D.quest_desc": [
    "&eRecharge Pedestals&r work to add &eVis&r to whatever Items you toss into them. \\n\\nWith &3Wands&r the &ePedestal&r will only take from &eNodes&r within 8 Blocks of it. \\n\\nWith other Items it will take from the &dAura&r instead of &eNodes&r.",
  ],
  "task.3592C011AFBE1091.title": "Wand Rods",
  "task.66C69842D25C128F.title": "Beds",
  "quest.1DCA32C5A690828A.quest_desc": [
    "&5Tainted Spore Stalks&r can't harm you... but their offspring can! \\n\\nOvertime they'll develop &5Taint Spores&r. Technically these are Mobs themselves but I didn't make the Kill Quest for them because they will almost immediately explode and release a dozen tiny &5Tainted&r Spiders! \\n\\nThese &5Taint Spiders&r are much smaller and &5purple-er&r? Than normal Spiders. They only have 2 and half &4Hearts&r. \\n\\nHow big the &5Taint Spore&r becomes determines how many will Spawn. ",
  ],
  "task.54AF5333615C3E4B.title": "Golem Body",
  "task.76951AB00CCA5DE3.title": "Golem Legs",
  "quest.225993D2A2868AF4.quest_desc": [
    "&3Wands&r are helpful for a lot, I mean come on it's a Magic Mod! \\n\\nFirst they hold &eVis&r. We can use it in an &2&lArcane Workbench&r to use the &eVis&r within the &3Wand&r instead of using &eVis Crystals&r. You can see it in the Top Left while Holding your &3Wand&r. Shifting will show the exact numbers. \\n\\nRunning low on &eVis&r? Just Shift Right Click to refill it... very slowly. Or you can use a Machine like a &eVis Recharger&r. \\n\\nWe can also use them with &3Foci&r (plural for &3Focus&r). Hold F while using your &3Wand&r and it will show the&3 Foci&r in your Inventory. You can Click them to add them to the &3Wand&r. \\n\\nRight Clicking the &3Wand&r will then use the &3Focus&r at the Cost at &eVis&r. You can just hold F and Left Click the &3Focus&r in the&3 Wand&r to remove it.",
  ],
  "quest.47FBC70FBC6C1E26.quest_subtitle": "Plant",
  "quest.08DD0CF854889F50.quest_desc": [
    "The &eThaumatorium&r is a very simple Multiblock Machine. \\n\\nJust place a &7&lCrucible&r, then 2 &eAlchemical Constructs&r towered above it. Give it some &dSalis Mundus&r and it will form the &eThaumatorium&r. \\n\\nYou can Pipe in &eEssentia&r automatically from &eEssentia Tubes&r and it won't need &bWater&r added to it, only a &cHeat Source&r below it. \\n\\nIn order to actually use it, Open its GUI and you can place an Item in it for certain Recipes. Then, you'll need to select which Recipe you want to be made and it will automatically create them. \\n\\nIt will either toss the Items it creates out or if there's an Inventory connected to it it will put the Items into it.",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/thaumaturge/thaum_tower1.png width:50 height:100 align:center click_action:none:}",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/thaumaturge/thaum_tower2.png width:50 height:100 align:center click_action:none:}",
  ],
  "quest.5B46057669C87196.title": "&dSalis Mundus",
  "quest.2D331894D0DE32CB.title": "&5Eldritch Obelisks",
  "quest.615179FA7C209DE0.title": "&cGolem&r Legs",
  "quest.1A60EA7CB3C600B5.title": "&eEssentia Crystallizer",
  "quest.3403790B54D114D4.title": "&7Golemancer's Bell",
  "task.45B781EC265A0618.title": "Golem Arms",
  "task.454C36CC76416460.title": "Elemental Tools",
  "quest.19932A116C8EE714.quest_desc": [
    "&5Taintacles&r are rare Mobs spawning from &5Tainted&r areas. \\n\\nThey have 50 &4Hearts&r and pose a much bigger threat than the previous Mobs. \\n\\nWell, that is if you're standing very close to them. They're stuck where they Spawn and can't move from it, so if you aren't next to them then they aren't a threat. \\n\\nThey won't Drop anything on death...",
  ],
  "quest.29CC17333C92174E.quest_desc": [
    "The &8Primal Crusher&r is &5&lThaumaturges&r Paxel. \\n\\nMade with all the &8Void Tools&r it can mine a 3x3 of anything the &8Void Picks&f or &8Shovels&r would. It also does more Damage than any previous Weapons. \\n\\nLike other &8Void Tools&r it will automatically Repair itself over time. It also gives you &4Temporary Warp&r when you use it.",
  ],
  "quest.7B659C1D725BDEB2.title": "&6Goggles of Revealing",
  "quest.072217F29C63E436.quest_subtitle": "Protection",
  "quest.547259A485A7BDCA.quest_subtitle": "Flux",
  "quest.09FD966539DA9960.title": "&eEssentia Mirror",
  "quest.3E295FDDE2588EE8.title": "&aFabrico",
  "quest.7C0A663CFC8DDAC3.quest_subtitle": "Destruction",
  "quest.4262D93E6549DB51.title": "Biomes where &4Crimson Portals&r spawn",
  "quest.08F7DB9115F6525E.title": "&5&lArcane Infusion&r Instability",
  "quest.0873DA638744B889.title": "&6Thaumometer",
  "quest.27729CC2CC9E720B.title": "Collapsing &5&lFlux Rifts",
  "quest.39C080EE72182A8B.title": "Wireless &eEssentia&r?",
  "quest.521EE1FA4C016AAA.title": "&cGolem&r Arms",
  "quest.0082F33484A3C771.quest_subtitle": "Life",
  "quest.043C6D99048C3890.quest_desc": [
    "&8Eldritch Guardians&r Spawn from a few things. Insanity and Eldritch Rituals are the main way. \\n\\n&8Eldritch Guardians&r have 50 &4Hearts&r with 4 Armor Points. \\n\\nIf you're slightly far from them they will shoot magic balls at you that give some nasty Effects. Closer and they will just smack you. \\n\\nThey don't Drop Items, they are just a nuisance.",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/thaumaturge/thaum_guardian.png width:100 height:150 align:center click_action:none:}",
  ],
  "quest.4722F2533E8AE1C4.title": "&eAer",
  "quest.7BC7861D2AFF266C.quest_subtitle": "Fire",
  "quest.6958759ABD603C22.title": "&2Permutatio",
  "quest.29AA2F2E28439514.title": "&dEnergized Nodes",
  "quest.7C0A663CFC8DDAC3.title": "&8Perdito",
  "quest.18250BCA57DE2BBE.title": "&e&lResearch Table",
  "quest.3403790B54D114D4.quest_desc": [
    "The &7Golemancer's Bell&r is necessary to command &cGolems&r and set up &cControl Seals&r. \\n\\nWith &cGolems&r you can just Shift Right Click them by Hand to pick them up as Items. \\n\\nIf you Right Click on them with a &7Golemancer's Bell&r they'll ignore &cControl Seals&r and just follow you. Right Clicking them again will make them stay and go back to obeying &cControl Seals&r. \\n\\nRight Clicking a &cControl Seal&r with a &7Golemancer's Bell&r will open its settings. If they have them it'll be: Area, Filter, Options, Priority, and Requirements. The last is just Redstone Control, that's simple. \\n\\nArea is the working area of the &cGolem&r, like for picking up Items with Collect. Any Items within the Area the &cGolem&r will grab. You can change how big it is with each Axis! \\n\\nFilter determines what Items can or can't be used. I say can or can't because you can choose Whitelisting or Blacklisting. \\n\\nOptions only comes with specific &cAdvanced Seals&r. It takes the Filter part to a higher degree of what it is Filtering. \\n\\nPriority is where we choose the order the &cSeals&r are in. From -5 to 5. We can also choose if only our &cGolems&r can use the &cSeal&r or if only specific colors of &cGolems&r can. \\n\\nRequirements will tell what Traits a &cGolem&r can or can't use it. Forbidden means if a &cGolem&r has the Trait it can't use it. Required means the &cGolem&r needs the Trait in order to use it. ",
  ],
  "quest.490981D7402F1AA3.quest_subtitle": "Spirit",
  "quest.476556F0B06ADCA9.quest_subtitle": "Flight",
  "task.7CD6CBEC3E95D591.title": "Golem Head",
  "quest.33BD3ED3A86D00ED.title": "&6Alienis",
  "quest.6BEA915DB03C70E0.quest_desc": [
    "&bJars&r are like &dShulker Boxes&r for &eEssentia&r. \\n\\nYou can Right Click &bJars&r on &eAlembics&r to extract the &eEssentia&r or use &bPhials&r on &bJars&r to empty the &bPhial&r into the &bJar&r. \\n\\nEach &bJar&r can hold one type of &eEssentia&r and up to 250 (be default). You can Right Click them on the ground to place them. \\n\\nHeck you can even connect &eTubes&r to them!",
  ],
  "quest.0082F33484A3C771.title": "&cVictus",
  "quest.3B7679135A74BBBA.quest_desc": [
    "&2Angry Zombies&r spawn in 4s from Sinister Nodes. \\n\\nThey have 12 and a half &4Hearts&r and 4 Armor Points. \\n\\nThey deal more Damage than normal &2Zombies&r and they won't Burn in &eDaylight&r. \\n\\nThese &2Zombies&r might Drop their &2Brains&r.",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/thaumaturge/thaum_zombie.png width:100 height:150 align:center click_action:none:}",
  ],
  "quest.78E1B825B4E7B307.quest_desc": [
    "While wearing this Charm you'll get a &eVis&r Discount. \\n\\nHow much? Depends on how much &4Warp&r you have. \\n\\nThe more &4Permament Warp&r you have, the less &eVis&r you'll have to spend!",
  ],
  "quest.40157DBAE2058521.quest_desc": [
    "&5Thaumium Gear&r is made just like most Gear is, Ingots and Sticks for Tools. \\n\\nThe &5Sword &fand &5Spears&r Damage is between Iron and &bDiamond&r, while the &5Axe&r is actually less than both. \\n\\nThe &5Pickaxe&r is the same Tier as &bDiamond&r and every Tool is very easy to Enchant. \\n\\nAll 4 pieces of &5Thaumium Armor&r will give 15 Armor Points and 4 Armor Toughness.",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/thaumaturge/thaum_thaumium.png width:100 height:150 align:center click_action:none:}",
  ],
  "quest.18520C1B616641B4.title": "&zPrimordial Items",
  "quest.46EAA6889A904314.quest_subtitle": "Metal",
  "task.0ADC46AF57FB9128.title": "Wand Caps",
  "quest.7CA7F4F31BC570D3.quest_desc": [
    "&eEssentia Tubes&r are the Pipes for &5&lThaumaturge&r. (Check out &bMagical Forests&r to make Quicksilver) \\n\\n&eEssentia Tubes&r work on Suction from Machines and Storages they connect to. \\n\\nJust connect them from the automatic inputs and outputs of Machines and it will start moving &eEssentia&r. \\n\\nUsing a Wand on them or Shift Right Clicking will disconnect and reconnect them.",
  ],
  "quest.34027FB5DD7419C5.title": "&cAversio",
  "quest.1AFD7D4D8A73BD9F.title": "&aTerra",
  "quest.043C6D99048C3890.title": "&8Eldritch Guardians",
  "quest.1DCA32C5A690828A.title": "&5Taint Spores&r",
  "quest.08BD38B3ED25D0F7.title": "&8Void Thaumaturge Armor",
  "quest.0673AED417439C53.title": "Mound Structure",
  "quest.42A6111B27289BCF.quest_subtitle": "Movement",
  "quest.5170CC16613804DC.title": "&2&lArcane Workbench",
  "task.5A6AA8E5EF02B0D3.title": "Thaumium Fortress Armor",
  "quest.5643D8B1506FF9B8.quest_desc": [
    "&3Foci&r (plural of &3Focus&r) are used for making &3Spells&r! \\n\\nThey need to be attached to &3Wands&r in order to be used. Hold F while using your&3 Wand&r to open the menu to attach or remove a &3Focus&r. \\n\\nWe'll need a &3Focal Manipulator&r to actually make &3Spells&r, that's in the next Quest so hold your Horses. \\n\\nWe still need to explain that this is only a &3Lesser Focus&r, it has limits to the complexity of the &3Spells&r it holds. &3Upgraded Foci&r will have less problems with these.",
  ],
  "quest.76586B14AA42057C.title": "Getting rid of &5Flux",
  "quest.03ED04CD00BB0EF9.title": "&bWorkbench Charger",
  "quest.700125E6B9CDE180.quest_desc": [
    "The &bMagical Forest&r is a Biome added by &5&lThaumaturge&r. \\n\\nSome of them are pretty small... and rare. \\n\\nIf you happen to find one (especially one big enough) you can find unique Plant life.",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/thaumaturge/thaum_magical.png width:150 height:100 align:center click_action:none:}",
  ],
  "quest.7ABF6AC8890537EB.quest_subtitle": "Conscious",
  "quest.4262D93E6549DB51.quest_desc": [
    "Can't find a Mound Structure? You always can just walk around Dry Biomes like Deserts and Badlands. \\n\\n&4Crimson Portals&r might randomly spawn around these Biomes during the Day. \\n\\nThe &4Portal&r itself has 100 &4Hearts&r and it will Spawn &4Crimson Cultists&r, it will take Damage when it does. \\n\\nOnce the &4Portal&r runs out of Health it will despawn.",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/thaumaturge/thaum_portal.png width:100 height:120 align:center click_action:none:}",
  ],
  "quest.15D4C3A29910407F.title": "&cGolem&r Head",
  "quest.0873DA638744B889.quest_desc": [
    "Magic, magic everywhere. \\n\\nHolding out the &6Thaumometer&r and Holding Right Click on a Block will Research the Block. \\n\\nWhen a Block gets Researched you'll learn the &aAspects&r its made of and earn those &eAspects&r. \\n\\nThis doesn't just work on Blocks though, you can also Research Dropped Items and even Mobs! \\n\\nYou'll only start off learning the &eAspects&r you already know, the Primal ones. In order to find new ones you'll need to use the Research Table to learn them before using the &6Thaumometer&r to find them.",
  ],
  "quest.232DD7B67C334F1B.title": "&6Humanus",
  "quest.78E1B825B4E7B307.title": "&9Voidseer's Pearl",
  "quest.15D4C3A29910407F.quest_desc": [
    "The brain of the operations... literally. \\n\\nSmart Brains will increase the &cGolems&r IQ, at the cost of some Durability. No Brain and brawn here I guess. \\n\\nThe Armored Smart Brain keeps the Brain and the brawn. I guess it is possible! \\n\\nThe Perceptive Head is the same as a normal Brain, just with Glasses. \\n\\nAnd the Biothaumic Brain is like the Smart Brain just with Glasses.",
  ],
  "quest.40157DBAE2058521.title": "&5Thaumium Gear",
  "quest.5ED26FC38CD7DB7C.title": "&3Wand Rods",
  "quest.7CFEC5BFC58E382C.title": "&5Taint Seeds",
  "quest.49399AC18569034E.quest_desc": [
    "&8Void Metal&r can make a great bunch of Gear. Each Tool will regain Durability just when they aren't being used. But they also give you &4Temporary Warp&r when you're using them. \\n\\n&8Void Swords&r do the same Damage as &bDiamond Swords&r and &8Void Pickaxes&r are the same tier as &bDiamond Pickaxes&r. \\n\\nThe Armor gives 20 Armor Points and 4 Armor Points.",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/thaumaturge/thaum_voidarmor.png width:100 height:150 align:center click_action:none:}",
  ],
  "quest.15FF21AF6F1C8896.quest_subtitle": "Should it be that high?",
  "quest.28C11EC49ED2E4D3.title": "&4Crimson Cultists",
  "task.52ECDA3B81500D18.title": "Different Essentia Tubes",
  "quest.2BECD3C37FDD675F.quest_desc": [
    "&5Taint Crawlers&r are the first Mobs to usually spawn from &5Flux&r. They can also come from &5Taint Features&r. \\n\\nThey're tiny Endermite like bugs, that spawn &5Taint Fiber&r wherever they go. \\n\\nThey got 4 &4Hearts&r and don't Drop anything on Death. They will also infect you with &5Flux Taint&r when they Hit you.",
  ],
  "quest.10DBA28AAEA8FA25.quest_desc": [
    "&5Infusion&r is how we unlock the rest of the Recipes. To make the &5&lArcane Infuser&r we'll need 8 &7Arcane Stone&r, atleast 1 &7Arcane Pedestal&r, and the &5Runic Matrix&r. \\n\\nPlace down the &7Arcane Pedestal&r and diagonal from each side place down towers of 2 &7Arcane Stone&r. With a Block gap above the &7Pedestal&r, then place the &5Runic Matrix&r. \\n\\nTo form the Multiblock toss some &dSalis Mundus&r on it. If it worked the &7Arcane Stones&r will form &5Infusion Pillars&r, if not, somethings wrong with how you built it. To actually get it started though you'll need to use a &3Wand&r on the &5Runic Matrix&r. Once it is spinning it will be ready for Recipes! \\n\\nThis is when you'll need to place &bJars&r and more &7Pedestals&r around the &5&lArcane Infuser&r. The main Item for the Recipes will go on the middle &7Pedestal&r while the other Items will go in other &7Pedestals&r around it. The &bJars&r will need to hold the &eEssentia&r for Recipes. \\n\\nOnce all the Items and &eEssentia&r are ready they'll all be used up and brought to the middle... this is when Instability comes into play.",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/thaumaturge/thaum_infuser1.png width:100 height:100 align:center click_action:none:}",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/thaumaturge/thaum_infuser2.png width:100 height:100 align:center click_action:none:}",
  ],
  "quest.12D9E344D6B4AD77.title": "&5Thaumic Slimes",
  "task.395D51F229C646C3.title": "Thaumium Gear",
  "quest.75EFD75C1C7644B2.title": "&bShimmerleaf",
  "quest.075312A557578AE0.title": "&bVitreus",
  "quest.5B4F7764F0F8EC0C.quest_desc": [
    "The &c&lGolem Press&r is a Multiblock made of all these Blocks. \\n\\nPlace down the Piston with an Iron Bar above it. Next to the Piston we'll need a &7Stone Table&r North of it with a Cauldron East of it. Place an &7Anvil&r between the &7Table&r and &7Cauldron&r and finally finish it off with &dSalis Mundus&r. \\n\\nDon't worry, it doesn't get less complicated from here! \\n\\nHere we get a bunch of different options to build our &cGolems&r from. The Body, Upgrades, Head, Arms, and Legs. \\n\\nYou can use the arrows next to each option to change them. This will add different Effects you can see and read about in the middle. You can also see the specific details about the &cGolem&r in the bottom: Health, Armor, and Damage. \\n\\nOn the right you can see the Items needed to build the selected &cGolem&r. Toss all those Items in and you can start Processing the &cGolem&r, this is when you'll need to Pipe in &7Machina&r into where the Piston used to be. \\n\\nOnce finished, the &cGolem&r will be ready and made in the &c&lPress&r.",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/thaumaturge/thaum_press1.png width:100 height:100 align:center click_action:none:}",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/thaumaturge/thaum_press2.png width:100 height:100 align:center click_action:none:}",
  ],
  "quest.2CDB0970A097C0AC.title": "&6Bestia",
  "quest.19932A116C8EE714.quest_subtitle": "Taint tickles lol",
  "quest.7688896C886CBFF3.quest_desc": [
    "&2Zombie Brains&r can be used for a few Recipes. \\n\\nMostly ones needing some sort of thinking processings. \\n\\nYou can also eat them? This will give you &4Temporary Warp&r or normal &4Warp&r. \\n\\nI guess the &dAura&r isn't a fan of cannibalism.",
  ],
  "quest.579ACBFD4C70BBD2.quest_desc": [
    "&4Crimson Rites&r is a Book on the Eldritch. \\n\\nUnfortunately most of it is impossible for us to decipher. \\n\\nBut, some of it gives us enough of an idea to know where to start!",
  ],
  "quest.3E311C85E71F6E5E.quest_desc": [
    "&2Greatwood Trees&r look like if Oak just kept on growing. You know the big Oak Trees? Think of those. But bigger! \\n\\nThey need a 2x2 of Saplings to be regrown. \\n\\nThey spawn in many Forest Biomes and are fairly easy to find.",
  ],
  "quest.4722F2533E8AE1C4.quest_subtitle": "Air",
  "quest.1E939BEAA712D60D.title": "&3Wand Caps",
  "quest.05DDA9C6B7C7E18E.quest_desc": [
    "The &dArcane Spa&r makes making &6Purifying Fluid&r a breeze. \\n\\nToss in &dBath Salts&r and &bWater&r and it will consume one of both to generate &6Purifying Fluid&r above it. \\n\\nIt can fill a pool 5 Blocks around it with &6Purifying Fluid&r. \\n\\nIt doesn't just use &6Purifying Fluid&r though, you can Pipe in any Fluid (and switch its GUI to only use Fluid) and it will place down that Fluid.",
  ],
  "quest.26F5B01872848BCF.title": "&bAqua",
  "quest.10DBA28AAEA8FA25.title": "&5&lArcane Infuser",
  "task.0CADE0C7893C5B2D.title": "Vis Crystals",
  "quest.47FBC70FBC6C1E26.title": "&2Herba",
  "quest.5129A772037498EA.quest_subtitle": "Magic",
  "quest.0F311C523A9ADC5F.quest_subtitle": "Light",
  "quest.5B82CF209A6EF130.title": "&7&lCrucible",
  "quest.7EFC0C6396E0C483.title": "&2Elemental Tools",
  "quest.18520C1B616641B4.quest_desc": [
    "Very rare with giant &5&lFlux Rifts&r, when they collapse they might Drop a &zPrimordial Mote&r. \\n\\nWait... we need &zPrimordial Pearls&r not &zMotes&r... \\n\\nThankfully we can Craft &zPrimordial Motes&r into... &zPrimordial Nodules&r? \\n\\nStill not &zPearls&r! Guess we'll have to Craft them together again to get our &zPearls&r. \\n\\nThese are very pricey and only used in the best Recipes!",
  ],
  "quest.1E939BEAA712D60D.quest_desc": [
    "Half, or I guess 2/3rds, of a &3Wand&r is the &3Cap&r. \\n\\nEach &3Wand&r needs 2 &3Caps&r (of the same type) along with a &3Rod&r to Craft. \\n\\n&3Caps&r determine the &eVis Cost&r of &3Spells&r. 110% means we're spending more, 100% means we're spending the right amount, and less than 100% means we're getting it cheap! \\n\\nThe better the &3Cap&r, the less &eVis&r we'll spend. It's a Vis sale! \\n\\nThe cheapest &3Caps&r only need &2&lArcane Workbenches&r to Craft. The others will start out Inert and need Arcane Infusion to actually use them.",
  ],
  "quest.05DDA9C6B7C7E18E.title": "&dArcane Spa",
  "quest.34027FB5DD7419C5.quest_subtitle": "Hate",
  "quest.5B46057669C87196.quest_desc": [
    "A bit of &cRedstone&f, &8Flint&r, and 3 different types of &eVis Crystals&r in a Bowl will make &dSalis Mundus&r... \\n\\nNow what does it do? \\n\\n&dSalis Mundus&r is used to change Blocks and Items into new more Magical ones! \\n\\nThe Bookshelf into the &6&lThaumonomicon&r, Cauldron into &7&lCrucible&r, and Crafting Table into &2&lArcane Workbench&r.",
  ],
  "quest.3135F77E4AB99790.quest_desc": [
    "&dCausality Collapsers&r are very powerful (and explosive) Tools. \\n\\nWe'll need an &5&lArcane Infuser&r to make some. In the outer &7Pedestals&r we'll need 2 Nitor of any Color, 2 &cBlocks of Redstone&r, 2 Alumentum, a Morphic Resonator, and a Vis Resonator. Remember to keep them as Symmetric as possible! \\n\\nThe Item on the middle &7Pedestal&r will be &cTNT&r and we'll need a &bJar&r with 50 &6Alienis&r and another &bJar&r with 50 &5Vitium&r. \\n\\nThis Recipe is incredibly Unstable, so make sure your set up is Symmetrical with plenty of Items to help with Stability like &cStabilizers&r! \\n\\nIf it all works, you'll be granted a &dCausality Collapser&r, an Item that can be thrown to create an Explosion.",
  ],
  "quest.2D331894D0DE32CB.quest_desc": [
    "Eldritch Obelisks are another Structure that comes from &5&lThaumaturge&r. \\n\\nThey'll be needed for progressing through the Eldritch, hence the name. But for now we can just focus on the Mobs. \\n\\nEldritch Obelisks always spawn with a Sinister Node between the Altar and Obelisk itself. These can spawn &2Angry Zombies&r. \\n\\nThey can also spawn with &4Crimson Cultists&r around it!",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/thaumaturge/thaum_obselisk.png width:100 height:100 align:center click_action:none:}",
  ],
  "quest.4F6D870249CE2F17.title": "Nap time!",
  "quest.64BC60B57EEC509C.quest_desc": [
    "This Quest has been authored by &6AllTheMods Staff&r, or a &2Community contributor&r for use in AllTheMods Modpacks. ",
    "",
    "As all &6AllTheMods&r packs are licensed under &eAll Rights Reserved&r, this Quest is not allowed to be used in any public packs not released by &6AllTheMods Team&r without explicit permission. ",
    "",
    "This quest is intentionally hidden, if you're seeing this, you're in editing mode.",
  ],
  "quest.662F077AD22AEA1B.title": "&cGolem&r Upgrades",
  "quest.232DD7B67C334F1B.quest_subtitle": "Humanity",
  "quest.5ED26FC38CD7DB7C.quest_desc": [
    "&3Wand Rods&r are the structure of &3Wands&r. \\nEach &3Wand&r will need a &3Rod&r along with 2 &3Caps&r to Craft. \\n\\n&3Rods&r determine the amount of each &ePrimal Vis&r they hold by the Capacity. &eVis&r used for &3Spells&r and &2&lArcane Workbench&r Recipes. \\n\\nNormal Sticks only hold 25 of each Aspect, better Rods can hold more. Most will need Arcane Infusion to Craft though...",
  ],
  "quest.28C11EC49ED2E4D3.quest_desc": [
    "&4Crimson Portals&r will spawn 2 types of &4Crimson Cultists&r, the &4Crimson Knights &fand &4Crimson Clerics&r. \\n\\n&4Crimson Knights&r have 15 &4Hearts&r and 16 Armor Points. They weild an Iron Sword which they'll of course use to attack you. \\n\\n&4Crimson Clerics&r have 12 &4Hearts&r and 12 Armor Points. They will Shoot &cFireballs&r and Lightning Balls at you. \\n\\nBoth &4Knights&r and &4Clerics&r might Drop their Armor and on an even rarer occurance they might Drop the &4Crimson Rites&r. \\n\\nIf you use the &6Thaumometer&r to Research them, the &4Crimson Rites&r will have a greater Drop Rate.",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/thaumaturge/thaum_cleric.png width:100 height:150 align:center click_action:none:}",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/thaumaturge/thaum_knight.png width:100 height:150 align:center click_action:none:}",
  ],
  "quest.3F961CF0520B3AEB.quest_desc": [
    "You like the special effects the &2Elemental Tools&r get? \\n\\nWell lucky you! You can get some with &5Infusion Enchantments&r! \\n\\nI'm not going to list all of them, you've got a book for that. \\n\\nBut if you want to take off the &5Infusion Enchantment&r you'll need an &7Arcane Grindstone&r to do that.",
  ],
  "quest.3F961CF0520B3AEB.title": "&5Infusion Enchantments",
  "quest.5EE4441CED3C2D1D.title": "&dAura Nodes",
  "quest.15FF21AF6F1C8896.quest_desc": [
    "Pretty simple Tool, just hold it and it'll show a bar on the left side of your screen to show how much &4Warp&r you have. \\n\\nThe fuller it is... the worse your Sanity is.",
  ],
  "quest.74F8FF27C911E33F.title": "&bSilverwood Trees",
  "quest.7BED978C9F18F48A.quest_subtitle": "Senses",
  "quest.0673AED417439C53.quest_desc": [
    "Mounds are random Dungeons that spawn around the &2&lOverworld&r. A part of it might be sticking out. \\n\\nThey have a few Zombie and Skeleton Spawners, a &4Crimson Portal&r on the lowest floor, and always a Sinister Node. \\n\\nThe &4Crimson Portal&r will randomly spawn &4Crimson Cultists&r to Attack you. It has 100 &4Hearts&r and when it spawns &4Cultists&r or when you Hit it, it will lose Health. \\n\\nOnce it loses all of its Health it will explode and disappear!",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/thaumaturge/thaum_mound.png width:120 height:100 align:center click_action:none:}",
  ],
  "quest.56CA8FE4F47FD30E.quest_subtitle": "&eVis Crystals&r, these are legal!",
  "quest.5644DF859A83B0CB.quest_desc": [
    "&bPhials&r are another way of holding and moving &eEssentia&r. \\n\\n&bPhials&r can extract up to 10 of one type of &eEssentia&r. They can take from Machines like &eAlembics&r and give to Machines like &eCrystallizers&r. \\n\\nThey can also give and take from &bJars&r.",
  ],
  "quest.5998B1AFFDA09725.title": "&cSmelter&r Upgrades",
  "quest.700125E6B9CDE180.title": "&bMagical Forest",
  "quest.5B4F7764F0F8EC0C.title": "&c&lGolem Press",
  "quest.79762364D0FCC878.title": "&5Thaumium Essentia Smelter",
  "quest.5DD51B2E0D59AE90.quest_desc": [
    "The &8Deconstruction Table&r is a simple helpful Research Point Farm. \\n\\nWhen you put in an Item into the &8Table&r it will be destroyed and it will give one &ePrimal Aspect&r it is made of. \\n\\nLogs will give &bAqua &fand &aTerra&r, since they're made of &2Herba&r which is made of &cVictus &fand &aTerra&r. &cVictus&r being made of &bAqua &fand &aTerra&r.",
  ],
  "quest.190752598FDCE408.quest_desc": [
    "The Body mostly determines Weight, Health, and Armor for &cGolems&r. \\n\\n&2Greatwood&r and &6Brass&r are both Light. \\n\\n&cClay&r and &8Voidmetal&r are both normal Weight. \\n\\nIron and &5Thaumium&r are both Heavy. \\n\\n&cClay&f, Iron, and &5Thaumium&r are all Fire-proof while just Iron and &5Thaumium&r are Blast-proof. \\n\\n&8Voidmetal&r is the only one that will repair itself over time.",
  ],
  "quest.33BD3ED3A86D00ED.quest_subtitle": "Alien",
  "quest.32791F4495701E7A.title": "&4Vinculum",
  "quest.1A60EA7CB3C600B5.quest_desc": [
    "&eEssentia&r gets Piped in, &eVis Crystals&r come flying out!",
  ],
  "quest.16CAD00E5A2C2EC2.quest_desc": [
    "Just looking at &eEssentia Tubes&r doesn't tell much of what's going through or the Suction Value they have. \\n\\nMaking them out of Glass would fix the first issue, but that's also not possible. \\nUsing the Resonator will tell the Suction, what &eAspect&r, and how many. It also works on some Machines!",
  ],
  "quest.23CAD6414B20408A.title": "&7Machina",
  "quest.12D9E344D6B4AD77.quest_desc": [
    "&5Thaumic Slimes&r can Spawn when &5Flux Goo&r keeps getting out of control. \\n\\nThe &5Slimes&r have 4 different sizes. Small with half a &4Heart&r, Medium with 2, Large with 8, and Massive with 64! \\n\\nThe Smalls can't Damage you but the rest can, and when they do they'll give you &5Flux Taint&r. \\n\\nWhen Killed they might Drop &5Vitium Crystals&r.",
  ],
  "quest.10CB678409E37068.title": "&2Alkimia",
  "quest.3E295FDDE2588EE8.quest_subtitle": "Crafted",
  "quest.5129A772037498EA.title": "&5Praecantatio",
  "quest.08F0B67D02683C3A.title": "&cGolem Seals",
  "quest.5B698B4F90F859F5.title": "Different &eEssentia Tubes&r",
  "quest.56A0F8E3AE0C8ACF.title": "&dSanity Soap",
  "quest.6F4E1656EE7D9B1F.quest_subtitle": "Void",
  "task.479AF65AFA01FEF4.title": "AllRightsReserved",
}